    "description": "New Japan Chemical Co., Ltd. produces and sells chemical products in Japan and internationally. It provides oleo-chemicals, including hydrogenated oils, fatty acids and esters, glycerin, alcohols, non-ionic and anion surfactants, and amphoteric surfactants; and plasticizer, such as phthalate and non-phthalate plasticizers, and specialty plasticizers. The company also offers plastic and coating materials, which include clarifiers and nucleating agents, epoxy resin curing agent, epoxy resins, raw materials for resins, methacrylate, and antistatic agents; and lubricants, such as evaporation-resistant and low-viscosity lubricants, dibasic acid esters, and aromatic lubricants. In addition, it is involved in commissioned hydrogenation business. The company was incorporated in 1919 and is headquartered in Osaka, Japan."
